(duty-scheduler: fair door and auditorium duties for midweek and weekend
 meetings. This file owns the flags, the help text, the order of the
 steps, and the exit codes; every later file is named by the job it does.)

see "./roster.vox".
see "./calendar.vox".
see "./availability.vox".
see "./duties.vox".
see "./report.vox".

A flag called weeks is "-w" or "--weeks", it is a number with default 8.
A flag called 'names path' is "-f" or "--file", it is a text with default "names.txt".
A flag called 'start date as typed' is "-d" or "--start", it is a text.
A flag called 'grid path' is "-s" or "--schedule", it is a text with default "availability.csv".
A flag called 'wants an empty grid' is "-g" or "--gen", it is a boolean.
A flag called 'csv path' is "-o" or "--output", it is a text with default "schedule.csv".
A flag called 'wants help' is "-h" or "--help", it is a boolean.

Parse flags.

If 'wants help' then,
  Print "duty-scheduler: fair door and auditorium duties for midweek and weekend meetings",
  Print "",
  Print "Usage: scheduler [OPTIONS]",
  Print "  -f, --file <path>      Names file, one person per line (default: names.txt)",
  Print "  -w, --weeks <N>        Number of weeks to schedule (default: 8)",
  Print "  -d, --start <date>     Date of the first midweek meeting (default: the first",
  Print "                         midweek meeting day on or after the 1st of next month).",
  Print "                         Accepts 2026-07-29, 20260729, 29 Jul 2026, or a phrase",
  Print "                         such as \"next wednesday\".",
  Print "  -s, --schedule <path>  Availability grid CSV (default: availability.csv)",
  Print "  -g, --gen              Write an empty availability grid to the -s path and exit",
  Print "  -o, --output <path>    Schedule CSV to write (default: schedule.csv)",
  Print "  -h, --help             Show this help",
  Print "",
  Print "Grid format: a header row of \"Meeting\" then the names, then one row per meeting",
  Print "(midweek, weekend, midweek, ...) whose first cell is the meeting's label and",
  Print "whose other cells are 0 (available) or 1 (unavailable). Columns are matched",
  Print "to people by the header name, in any order. Example for three people, one week:",
  Print "  Meeting,Alice,Bob,Charlie",
  Print "  Wed 29 Jul 2026 midweek,0,1,0",
  Print "  Sun 2 Aug 2026 weekend,0,0,0",
  Exit 0.

If weeks is less than 1 then,
  Print "scheduler: --weeks must be at least 1",
  Exit 1.

'read the names from' with 'names path'.
the 'meeting count' is weeks multiply 2.
Set 'the first midweek moment' to 'the first midweek moment typed as' of 'start date as typed'.

If 'wants an empty grid' then, 'write an empty grid to' with 'grid path'.

'load the grid from' with 'grid path'.
'prepare the duties'.
'assign every duty'.

Print "Duty schedule".
Print "=============".
Print "People: {names's length}".
Print "Weeks: {weeks}".
Print "First midweek meeting: {'the long date of' of 'the first midweek moment'}".
Print "Availability: {'the availability note'}".

'print the schedule'.
'print the summary'.
'write the csv to' with 'csv path'.
